problems.problem:
Let $\mathbb{N}$ be the set of nonnegative integers and $\mathbb{Z}$ the set of all integers. A function $f : \mathbb{N} \times \mathbb{Z} \to \mathbb{Z}$ satisfies

(i) $f(0, 0) = 1$, $f(0, 1) = 1$;

(ii) $f(0, k) = 0$ for every $k \notin \{0, 1\}$;

(iii) $f(n, k) = f(n-1, k) + f(n-1, k-2n)$ for all $n \ge 1$ and all $k$.

Find the value of the sum
$$\sum_{k=0}^{\binom{2009}{2}} f(2008, k).$$

Find all functions $f : \mathbb{R}^+ \to \mathbb{R}^+$ such that
$$\left\{\frac{f(x)}{f(y)}\right\} + \left\{\frac{f(y)}{f(z)}\right\} + \left\{\frac{f(z)}{f(x)}\right\} = \left\{\frac{x}{y}\right\} + \left\{\frac{y}{z}\right\} + \left\{\frac{z}{x}\right\}$$
for all $x, y, z \in \mathbb{R}^+$. (For a real number $x$, $\{x\} = x - \lfloor x \rfloor$, where $\lfloor x \rfloor$ is the integer part of $x$; e.g. $\{2.7\} = 0.7$ and $\{4\} = 0$.)

Let $a$ and $b$ be given real numbers. Find all functions $f : \mathbb{R} \to \mathbb{R}$ such that
$$f\left(x + f^{100}(y) + a\right) = y + f^{2025}(x) + b$$
for all $x, y \in \mathbb{R}$. (For a positive integer $k$, $f^k(x) = f(f(\cdots f(x)))$ with $f$ applied $k$ times.)
